WEBVTT

00:05.640 --> 00:09.394
I'd like to propose a toast
to my beautiful bride-to-be.

00:09.920 --> 00:12.354
Darling,
I never thought I'd find love again.

00:12.520 --> 00:16.638
I not only found it,
but I found the love of my life.

00:16.800 --> 00:17.869
To Evelyn.

00:18.040 --> 00:19.632
- Hear, hear.
- Hear, hear.

00:20.040 --> 00:22.600
That poor, clueless bastard.

00:23.120 --> 00:26.829
It's like watching a dog
stick his face in a fan.

00:27.000 --> 00:29.070
You don't do that more than once.

00:31.720 --> 00:34.632
I am the lucky one in this relationship.

00:34.800 --> 00:36.279
And I promise you, darling...

00:36.440 --> 00:41.275
...I am going to be the best wife
I possibly can.

00:41.440 --> 00:42.429
To Teddy.

00:42.600 --> 00:43.953
- Teddy.
- To Teddy.

00:44.120 --> 00:46.634
That poor, clueless bastard.

00:47.480 --> 00:50.040
- So can we go now?
- No, we can't. It would be rude.

00:50.200 --> 00:51.235
I don't mind being rude.

00:51.720 --> 00:53.472
You just talking or you got a plan?

00:53.920 --> 00:56.480
Well, if I eat enough shrimp,
I can make myself puke.

00:56.640 --> 00:57.629
Then start eating.

00:57.800 --> 01:00.109
Okay, stop it, both of you.
There will be no puking.

01:00.280 --> 01:02.430
We're gonna stay,
congratulate the happy couple...

01:02.600 --> 01:05.194
...mingle a bit,
and then I'm gonna fake a migraine.

01:05.760 --> 01:07.159
- You can do that?
- Hell, yeah.

01:07.320 --> 01:10.835
I spent 12 years watching my wife
fake migraines and orgasms.

01:11.640 --> 01:12.993
I'd go with the migraine.

01:15.080 --> 01:17.071
Thanks for coming, fellas.
Means a lot to me.

01:17.840 --> 01:18.829
Wouldn't miss it.

01:19.000 --> 01:22.151
We wish you a lifetime
of love and happiness. Right, Charlie?

01:22.320 --> 01:25.790
Well, yeah, but he seems
hell-bent on marrying Mom.

01:26.240 --> 01:28.674
Hey, Daddy. Sorry I'm late.

01:28.840 --> 01:30.034
That's okay, doodlebug.

01:30.440 --> 01:32.590
Just glad you could make it.

01:33.640 --> 01:36.996
Charlie, Alan, Jake,
this is my daughter, Courtney.

01:37.160 --> 01:39.390
Honey,
these are Evelyn's sons and grandson.

01:39.800 --> 01:40.835
I'm the grandson.

01:41.240 --> 01:45.153
- Oh, well, it's nice to finally meet you all.
- Nice to meet you too.

01:45.320 --> 01:46.719
So, Teddy, what's the deal?

01:46.880 --> 01:49.792
All this time, you've been hiding
this beautiful woman from us?

01:50.280 --> 01:52.510
Just from you, Charlie.

01:53.160 --> 01:55.628
- Fair enough.
- Dad's a little overprotective.

01:56.040 --> 01:57.234
I can see why.

01:57.640 --> 02:00.359
Charlie, why don't you and I
get Courtney a drink?

02:00.520 --> 02:02.909
I'd like to get Courtney a house.

02:03.480 --> 02:05.436
Walk with me.

02:06.320 --> 02:08.675
- How's your headache, Dad?
- Not yet. So...

02:10.360 --> 02:14.035
Courtney, you have amazing posture.
Do you see a chiropractor?

02:14.560 --> 02:17.028
- No.
- Would you like to?

02:17.720 --> 02:21.315
- Charlie, I need you to do me a favor.
- Anything for you, Teddy. Name it.

02:21.480 --> 02:24.597
- Stay away from Courtney.
- Name something else.

02:25.000 --> 02:26.831
- Charlie, this is important.
- Don't worry.

02:27.000 --> 02:29.389
I think too much of you
to wanna, you know...

02:29.560 --> 02:31.710
...do what I wanna do
with your daughter.

02:32.520 --> 02:34.750
- I appreciate that.
- Consider it a wedding present.

02:35.160 --> 02:37.628
- Thanks.
- No, seriously, that's all you get.

02:39.760 --> 02:41.876
Courtney, dear,
what a surprise to see you.

02:42.040 --> 02:46.158
- Well, I told you I was coming.
- Yes, but the party started an hour ago.

02:46.320 --> 02:49.676
So I naturally assumed that something
had come up that was more important...

02:49.840 --> 02:51.239
...than your father's happiness.

02:52.680 --> 02:55.433
Well, Evelyn, you know
what they say about assuming.

02:55.600 --> 02:58.956
When you assume, you're just a bitch.

02:59.720 --> 03:04.191
- Courtney, there are children present.
- She means me, but I'm fine with it.

03:05.120 --> 03:06.109
Thank you, dear.

03:06.280 --> 03:08.555
You should hear
what they call her at home.

03:09.280 --> 03:11.589
- Have some shrimp.
- Oh, boy.

03:12.040 --> 03:15.715
- Well, great party, but we gotta go.
- Oh, already?

03:15.880 --> 03:18.474
Yeah. We'd love to stay,
but Alan's got a headache.

03:18.640 --> 03:20.198
Not yet.

03:21.080 --> 03:24.197
Not yet debilitating,
but I do need to lay down.

03:24.360 --> 03:28.751
Hey, before you go, my dad
had mentioned that you like nice cars.

03:29.160 --> 03:30.354
- Yeah.
- I do too.

03:31.840 --> 03:33.114
Swell.

03:33.280 --> 03:35.794
Here's my card.
Maybe I can help you out someday.

03:35.960 --> 03:38.110
Whoa, Ferraris, Lamborghinis.

03:38.280 --> 03:42.068
They say driving one is the most fun
you can have with your pants on.

03:43.560 --> 03:47.553
Well, that's how I like to drive.
With my pants on.

03:47.720 --> 03:50.439
Otherwise,
the leather kind of sticks to my thighs.

03:50.600 --> 03:53.398
Well, you should come down sometime.
I'll give you a test drive.

03:53.800 --> 03:57.952
- Actually, I'm really not a Ferrari guy.
- I'm not either.

03:59.880 --> 04:01.199
- Bye.
- Bye-bye.

04:01.360 --> 04:04.670
We really gotta get our signals straight.
I mean, you made me look stupid.

04:04.960 --> 04:07.235
Don't blame your father for that.

04:08.360 --> 04:11.875
I'm telling you right now,
I'm not having any more children.

04:13.080 --> 04:14.798
Terrific.

04:46.520 --> 04:47.839
Hello?

04:48.000 --> 04:49.718
No, it's Alan.

04:50.280 --> 04:52.032
Oh, hi, Courtney.

04:52.320 --> 04:55.357
Well, it was very nice
meeting you last night too.

04:56.280 --> 04:57.269
Oh, I'm sorry...

04:57.440 --> 05:01.672
...I had no idea that you were planning
on using a fake migraine to get out early.

05:02.960 --> 05:05.269
So, what did you do?

05:05.800 --> 05:07.836
Menstrual cramps.

05:08.480 --> 05:10.630
Yeah, I can't get away with that.

05:11.160 --> 05:13.833
Although sometimes
I'll use irritable bowel syndrome.

05:14.000 --> 05:15.319
And...

05:16.160 --> 05:17.957
Okay, I'll get Charlie.

05:20.000 --> 05:22.230
It's Teddy's daughter.
She wants to talk to you.

05:22.400 --> 05:24.595
- Really?
- You promised Teddy you'd stay away.

05:24.760 --> 05:26.512
Hey, I didn't tell her to call me.

05:26.680 --> 05:29.148
What kind of man
would hit on his future stepsister?

05:30.600 --> 05:33.114
You're just making it hotter for him.

05:34.840 --> 05:36.876
Give me the phone, give me the phone.

05:38.200 --> 05:39.633
Hi, Courtney, what's up?

05:41.000 --> 05:44.151
That's nice, but I told you,
I'm really not into Ferraris.

05:45.200 --> 05:49.193
A Bentley?
Oh, it's a little more my style.

05:49.400 --> 05:51.960
Okay, I guess I could come by
and take a peek at it.

05:52.120 --> 05:53.872
First a peek, then a poke.

06:00.800 --> 06:02.552
Uncalled for.

06:04.800 --> 06:07.633
Two o'clock? Great. I'll see you then.

06:12.320 --> 06:14.356
I swear this is just business.

06:15.160 --> 06:17.628
I'm going to look at a Bentley
she got in on trade.

06:17.800 --> 06:19.631
I can get it for dealer cost.

06:19.800 --> 06:22.917
- Since when do you need a Bentley?
- Nobody needs a Bentley, Alan.

06:23.080 --> 06:25.833
Just like nobody needs
to date a woman half their age.

06:26.000 --> 06:28.434
But if you want one,
it doesn't hurt to have the other.

06:32.240 --> 06:34.595
Did Teddy tell you
to stay away from his daughter too?

06:34.760 --> 06:37.718
- No.
- Yeah, why would he?

06:48.480 --> 06:50.436
Pretty hot, isn't it?

06:50.960 --> 06:53.872
Oh, yeah. But it's not really my thing.

06:54.040 --> 06:56.713
Gee, I think a guy like you
would look great in one of these.

06:56.880 --> 06:58.233
- You think?
- Absolutely.

06:58.720 --> 07:02.554
Here. Slide on into it. See how it feels.

07:04.840 --> 07:05.955
What about the Bentley?

07:06.120 --> 07:09.829
I got the guys in the back washing it up
for you. We have a few minutes.

07:10.000 --> 07:11.035
Sure, why not.

07:11.720 --> 07:13.597
That's always been my motto.

07:17.240 --> 07:18.992
Oh, pretty snug.

07:20.000 --> 07:21.592
Tight's good, don't you think?

07:25.240 --> 07:27.435
Sure, tight's good.

07:30.840 --> 07:32.193
Oh, hi.

07:32.880 --> 07:34.313
Hi.

07:34.840 --> 07:36.956
So where do they put the engine
in these things?

07:37.120 --> 07:40.317
They put it where it belongs. In the rear.

07:50.160 --> 07:52.628
- So no stick?
- No, you shift from the wheel.

07:52.800 --> 07:54.074
Let me show you.

07:54.240 --> 07:56.959
Left side down, right side up.

07:57.640 --> 07:59.596
You don't need a stick.

07:59.760 --> 08:01.830
And yet I've got one anyway.

08:08.160 --> 08:10.435
- Is that your cell phone?
- Boy, I hope so.

08:12.280 --> 08:14.032
Excuse me.

08:14.360 --> 08:15.349
Hello?

08:15.520 --> 08:19.832
Oh, hey, hey, hey. Teddy, how are you?

08:21.200 --> 08:23.873
Good. Me? I'm fine.

08:24.480 --> 08:27.358
Just running some errands.

08:27.560 --> 08:30.836
Yeah, I'll be around tomorrow.
Drop by anytime.

08:31.000 --> 08:32.433
Great. I'll see you then.

08:34.240 --> 08:36.117
That was your dad.

08:37.720 --> 08:39.870
He wants to talk to me and Alan
about something.

08:40.040 --> 08:41.314
I heard.

08:41.480 --> 08:45.792
- Has he ever said anything about me?
- You? Let me think.

08:45.960 --> 08:48.155
He told you to stay away from me,
didn't he?

08:48.600 --> 08:49.715
Oh, yeah, there was that.

08:52.000 --> 08:54.309
I can't believe
he's still trying to control my life.

08:54.480 --> 08:56.277
Hey, your dad loves you.

08:56.440 --> 09:00.115
He's just trying to protect you from,
well, in this case, me.

09:01.960 --> 09:04.997
I'm a big girl, Charlie,
I can take care of myself.

09:05.440 --> 09:06.589
I'm sure you can.

09:07.880 --> 09:11.793
I can also take care of
whoever I choose to be with.

09:11.960 --> 09:13.916
I'm sure you can.

09:20.320 --> 09:25.110
Listen, I appreciate the offer,
but I think I'm gonna pass.

09:25.280 --> 09:26.679
On the Bentley.

09:28.440 --> 09:30.396
But you haven't even seen it yet.

09:30.560 --> 09:35.315
And right now, it's all wet and soapy,
just waiting for you.

09:42.880 --> 09:45.269
Are we still talking about a car?

09:47.360 --> 09:48.634
What do you think?

09:49.600 --> 09:53.070
I think I should probably get out
before I set off the air bag.

09:57.520 --> 10:02.469
And then she leaned over real close
to play with the... paddles.

10:03.240 --> 10:04.559
The what?

10:04.720 --> 10:06.551
The paddle shifters
on the steering wheel.

10:08.840 --> 10:11.195
I had another picture entirely.

10:13.920 --> 10:15.353
But I restrained myself.

10:15.520 --> 10:18.398
I walked away,
and now I can still look Teddy in the eye.

10:18.840 --> 10:19.875
That's great.

10:20.040 --> 10:22.554
But how come you have no problem
looking me in the eye...

10:22.720 --> 10:26.508
...after sleeping with my wife's sister,
my son's teacher, my divorce lawyer...

10:26.680 --> 10:28.113
...and my old receptionist?

10:29.160 --> 10:30.513
I like Teddy.

10:33.800 --> 10:36.439
- And the receptionist was your fault.
- How?

10:37.400 --> 10:40.312
If you'd paid her a decent salary,
she wouldn't have had to hook.

10:45.720 --> 10:47.312
I brought the Bentley.

10:47.720 --> 10:49.950
Come on, Courtney. I told you I can't.

10:50.440 --> 10:54.274
Just one little test drive.
What do you have to lose?

10:54.800 --> 10:58.554
Well, there's my integrity, my self
respect, my relationship with your father...

10:58.720 --> 11:00.631
Give me the damn keys.

11:05.520 --> 11:07.556
Is your brother still in bed
with his sister?

11:14.000 --> 11:15.752
Stepsister.

11:16.760 --> 11:18.193
To-be.

11:19.000 --> 11:20.638
And yes.

11:21.080 --> 11:22.479
Wow, how long has it been?

11:24.240 --> 11:25.673
About 18 hours.

11:26.360 --> 11:28.157
Good thing he's got supplies up there.

11:29.160 --> 11:31.071
- He does?
- Sure.

11:31.240 --> 11:34.915
Water, power bars, fresh batteries, rope.

11:36.120 --> 11:37.439
Oh, like an earthquake kit.

11:40.160 --> 11:42.993
I guess you could use that stuff
for earthquakes.

11:51.480 --> 11:53.072
Oh, crap.

11:56.240 --> 11:58.800
Misdirected anger. You'll get used to it.

11:59.240 --> 12:02.516
- What are you guys doing here?
- We came to talk with you and Charlie.

12:02.680 --> 12:03.749
Didn't he tell you?

12:03.920 --> 12:07.959
He never tells me anything. I don't know
half of what he does nor do I want to.

12:08.120 --> 12:11.476
It's his life and he alone should suffer
the consequences. Come on in.

12:13.920 --> 12:16.673
- Is he even home?
- I'll check.

12:16.840 --> 12:19.877
Why don't you make yourselves
comfortable...

12:20.240 --> 12:21.389
...and I'll check.

12:23.480 --> 12:25.152
Because I have no idea.

12:26.480 --> 12:29.153
So I'll need to check.

12:35.400 --> 12:36.515
Is he on something?

12:37.120 --> 12:38.997
If only.

12:42.080 --> 12:43.559
What?

12:44.760 --> 12:46.352
Teddy and Mom are downstairs.

12:46.520 --> 12:49.557
- What the hell are they doing here?
- Apparently, you invited them.

12:49.720 --> 12:51.199
- I did not.
- Yes, you did.

12:51.360 --> 12:52.952
On the phone, remember? Hey, Alan.

12:53.120 --> 12:55.680
Hi, Courtney, how are you doing?
Charlie, they're waiting.

12:56.200 --> 12:57.758
Yeah, we got a problem here.

12:57.920 --> 13:01.117
No, sir, you've got a problem.
I made no promise, I broke no promise.

13:01.280 --> 13:02.838
- You actually made a promise?
- Yeah.

13:03.000 --> 13:05.389
- And I really tried to keep it.
- He did.

13:05.560 --> 13:09.473
I could sense his inner conflict as we
did it in the back seat of the Bentley.

13:12.280 --> 13:14.589
Look, just stall them. I'll be right down.

13:14.760 --> 13:17.479
Fine. But know this,
I am not taking the fall for you.

13:17.640 --> 13:19.870
- How could you take the fall for me?
- I don't know.

13:20.040 --> 13:23.157
But it always seems to work out
that when you get laid, I get screwed.

13:25.000 --> 13:26.035
Just go.

13:27.560 --> 13:30.791
- Great. Just great.
- Hey, have you seen my dress?

13:31.440 --> 13:33.874
- Why?
- I ain't going down like this.

13:35.000 --> 13:36.752
You're not going down at all.

13:37.840 --> 13:40.559
Why not?
I have nothing to be ashamed of.

13:41.320 --> 13:43.788
Here, hit rewind.
I'm sure you'll find something.

13:49.560 --> 13:51.312
I just can't believe he's still in bed.

13:51.480 --> 13:53.232
He's a drunk, Mom.
That's what they do.

13:53.680 --> 13:55.477
Oh, come on, Evelyn,
give the kid a break.

13:55.640 --> 13:58.108
He was probably out late last night
sowing wild oats.

13:58.520 --> 14:01.478
He's 40 years old,
he has no more wild oats.

14:01.640 --> 14:04.200
Just warmed-over cream of wheat.

14:04.600 --> 14:07.319
Hey, hey, look who's here.

14:07.480 --> 14:10.040
Well, thanks for interrupting
your stupor and joining us.

14:10.200 --> 14:13.476
I can get back to my stupor anytime.
So, what's going on?

14:14.000 --> 14:16.230
Your mother and I wanted to
talk about the wedding.

14:16.400 --> 14:18.516
You've got my blessing. What else?

14:18.680 --> 14:21.399
Well, we wondered if you would mind
having the ceremony here.

14:21.560 --> 14:22.549
Sure. Terrific.

14:22.720 --> 14:25.598
On the deck, in here, on the beach,
wherever you want. What else?

14:25.920 --> 14:27.319
Don't you wanna think about it?

14:27.480 --> 14:30.597
What's to think about? It's perfect.
Have the ceremony, the reception.

14:30.760 --> 14:34.878
Alan and I'll clear out. You can use this
place for your honeymoon. It's broken in.

14:35.040 --> 14:36.109
The house, not Mom.

14:42.840 --> 14:45.752
Do you have one of your
little pop tarts up there?

14:46.160 --> 14:49.311
No, no, just my alarm.
If I'm not up by 4 in the afternoon...

14:49.480 --> 14:52.756
...I feel like I've wasted the whole day.
Be right back.

14:58.400 --> 15:00.311
- What do you think you're doing?
- I'm bored.

15:00.880 --> 15:03.440
- You're bored?
- Yeah. I wanna go downstairs.

15:03.600 --> 15:06.512
No, no, no, you can't go downstairs.
Find something else to do.

15:06.680 --> 15:09.240
Well, I'd love to sell you a car.

15:11.400 --> 15:12.628
Yeah, very funny.

15:13.840 --> 15:15.193
No, I'm serious.

15:16.800 --> 15:18.313
You wanna sell me a car now?

15:18.840 --> 15:21.798
Or I could go downstairs.

15:21.960 --> 15:23.791
You wouldn't.

15:23.960 --> 15:25.552
I would.

15:26.760 --> 15:28.557
Wait a minute.

15:28.720 --> 15:31.678
You planned this.
You knew they were coming over today.

15:31.840 --> 15:34.354
Well, a good salesman pays attention.

15:34.520 --> 15:37.512
- Now, if you'll excuse me.
- Okay, okay, okay, you win.

15:37.920 --> 15:40.912
- Give me a price on the Bentley.
- The Bentley's no longer available.

15:41.080 --> 15:42.832
I'm thinking the Ferrari.

15:43.800 --> 15:46.712
- I don't want a Ferrari.
- And I don't want to stay up here.

15:46.880 --> 15:50.236
- Charlie, we're waiting.
- Coming.

15:50.400 --> 15:51.719
Okay, fine.

15:52.720 --> 15:56.599
But let me just say,
this is no way to treat family.

15:57.720 --> 16:00.109
Here we go, blue eyes.

16:00.280 --> 16:02.510
- I made it myself.
- Oh, thank you.

16:02.680 --> 16:06.070
- Nothing for me, thanks.
- I don't recall offering.

16:08.120 --> 16:10.031
Sorry, sorry.

16:10.200 --> 16:13.397
So, wedding on the beach. Great.
I'll take care of everything.

16:13.560 --> 16:16.677
- Thanks for stopping by.
- Well, there is one more thing.

16:17.120 --> 16:18.348
- Name it.
- Well...

16:18.520 --> 16:22.195
Excuse me.
Berta, this is a family matter.

16:25.240 --> 16:26.798
If you only knew.

16:28.960 --> 16:30.552
Here's the deal.

16:30.720 --> 16:33.553
I never had any sons of my own,
just the one daughter.

16:33.720 --> 16:36.598
- And she's great. Isn't she great, Alan?
- Well, I hardly met her.

16:36.760 --> 16:39.911
- Me neither. I'm sure she's great.
- She's terrific.

16:40.080 --> 16:42.310
But I've grown very fond
of the two of you.

16:42.480 --> 16:46.393
And I'd like to ask you to stand up
with me when I marry your mother.

16:48.360 --> 16:52.876
- Teddy, that's quite an honor.
- Yeah. I'm really touched.

16:56.680 --> 16:59.240
Snooze button.
I must have hit the snooze button.

16:59.400 --> 17:00.913
Excuse me.

17:03.560 --> 17:06.711
I don't use the snooze button.
When I'm up, I'm up.

17:08.800 --> 17:10.028
Of course, I'm not a drunk.

17:15.480 --> 17:16.629
Are you out of your mind?

17:17.440 --> 17:21.433
I prefer to think of myself as a go-getter.
All right, now you're gonna wanna...

17:21.600 --> 17:24.751
...sign here, here, here,
and initial where the little flags are.

17:26.040 --> 17:28.600
This is twice as much as the Bentley.
I can't afford this.

17:29.240 --> 17:31.276
Well, if you need help
with the down payment...

17:31.440 --> 17:35.433
...I'm sure I could ask my dad
to help you out. He really loves you.

17:40.400 --> 17:41.549
Fine.

17:42.360 --> 17:45.158
Here. And here. And here.

17:45.320 --> 17:47.072
And here. And here.

17:47.520 --> 17:49.636
- What's this?
- Oh, that's the extended warranty.

17:49.800 --> 17:52.075
Just a little extra protection.

17:52.240 --> 17:54.435
I think it's a bit late for that.

17:55.080 --> 17:57.594
Congratulations. You now own a Ferrari.

17:58.360 --> 17:59.679
Yippee.

18:01.080 --> 18:02.672
Charlie.

18:03.280 --> 18:04.269
What now?

18:05.480 --> 18:06.913
I'm gonna need a check.

18:13.400 --> 18:16.551
You know, this is the most
I have ever spent for sex.

18:19.240 --> 18:20.753
But not by much.

18:26.520 --> 18:28.750
Okay, Mom,
I guess I'll see you at the wedding.

18:28.920 --> 18:30.831
Charlie, the wedding
isn't for six months.

18:31.000 --> 18:33.798
Yeah, but it's bad luck
to see the bride beforehand.

18:33.960 --> 18:37.396
Thanks again, fellas. You being a part
of this shindig means a lot to me.

18:37.560 --> 18:39.152
Our pleasure, Teddy. Bye-bye.

18:41.720 --> 18:44.280
Congratulations.
Once again, you get off scot-free.

18:44.440 --> 18:46.670
Free? You think that was free?

18:47.760 --> 18:49.318
- Charlie.
- Yeah, hey, hi.

18:49.480 --> 18:51.630
I wanted you to know
I'm not gonna say anything...

18:51.800 --> 18:53.791
...about you and Courtney.
They don't get along.

18:53.960 --> 18:56.428
Okay, great. Wait, wait, wait.

18:56.600 --> 18:57.794
You knew? How did you know?

18:58.280 --> 19:00.999
I just noticed the car outside
with her dealer plates on it.

19:01.440 --> 19:04.034
You couldn't have noticed that
on the way in?

19:05.160 --> 19:07.879
- How much did she take you for?
- Don't ask.

19:08.040 --> 19:11.715
- Well, you can't say I didn't warn you.
- Wait, wait, wait.

19:11.880 --> 19:14.269
So you were trying to protect me?

19:14.680 --> 19:16.716
Hey, you're a good kid.

19:16.880 --> 19:21.795
And Courtney, well, I love her,
but she is kind of a sociopath.

19:22.400 --> 19:23.389
Bye now.

19:27.720 --> 19:29.870
- You know what this means, don't you?
- What?

19:30.040 --> 19:32.634
I'm gonna need an eight-car garage.

19:57.080 --> 19:59.071
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

19:59.240 --> 20:01.231
[ENGLISH]
